        content: `British and Russian geologists conducted initial surveys identifying mineral potential across Afghanistan. Working with limited infrastructure and challenging political conditions, they nonetheless produced the first modern geological maps and descriptions of Afghan mineral occurrences. Their work documented coal basins, copper showings, iron prospects, and gemstone districts that would later become targets for detailed exploration.`,
