    title: 'Lithium Discovery & Exploration History',
    subtitle: 'Historical Exploration Leading to World\'s Largest Lithium Reserves',
    
    overview: `Lithium exploration in Afghanistan represents one of the most significant mineral discoveries of the 21st century, with geological surveys identifying potentially the world's largest lithium reserves in Ghazni Province. Initial estimates indicate 215 million metric tons of lithium carbonate equivalent—enough to supply global demand for centuries. Historical pegmatite mining in the region provided foundation for lithium discovery, with traditional gemstone extraction revealing lithium-bearing formations. Modern geological surveys combining satellite imagery, geophysical surveys, and drilling have revealed extensive pegmatite fields containing spodumene and lepidolite—primary lithium minerals essential for battery production. The discovery positions Afghanistan at the center of the global energy transition, with lithium reserves potentially supplying electric vehicle and energy storage markets for decades. Historical mining knowledge informed exploration strategies, while traditional understanding of pegmatite formations guided modern discovery efforts.`,
    stats: [
      { value: '215M Tons', label: 'Lithium Reserves', description: 'Carbonate equivalent' },
      { value: '#1 Global', label: 'Ranking', description: 'Largest reserves' },
      { value: 'Ghazni', label: 'Province', description: 'Primary deposits' },
      { value: 'Pegmatites', label: 'Formation', description: 'Lithium-bearing' },
      { value: 'Battery Grade', label: 'Quality', description: 'Premium material' },
      { value: 'Energy Transition', label: 'Impact', description: 'Global significance' }],
    sections: [
      {
        title: 'Historical Pegmatite Mining & Discovery Foundation',
        content: `Historical pegmatite mining in Ghazni and surrounding provinces provided foundation for lithium discovery, with traditional gemstone extraction revealing lithium-bearing formations. Artisanal miners working pegmatite deposits for tourmaline, aquamarine, and other gemstones encountered spodumene crystals—primary lithium minerals—though their significance was not recognized historically. Traditional knowledge of pegmatite formations and gemstone locations informed modern exploration strategies, with historical mining sites guiding geological surveys. The historical legacy of pegmatite mining demonstrates Afghanistan's geological diversity, while traditional knowledge provided foundation for modern lithium discovery.`,
        icon: Gem,
        alignment: 'left'
      },
      {
        title: 'Modern Discovery: World\'s Largest Lithium Reserves',
        content: `Modern geological surveys combining satellite imagery, geophysical surveys, and drilling have revealed extensive pegmatite fields containing world-class lithium reserves. Initial estimates indicate 215 million metric tons of lithium carbonate equivalent—potentially the world's largest reserves—with Ghazni Province hosting primary deposits. Spodumene and lepidolite crystals contain up to 8% lithium oxide, among the highest grades globally, suitable for battery-grade production. The discovery positions Afghanistan at the center of the global energy transition, with reserves potentially supplying electric vehicle and energy storage markets for decades. Modern exploration builds upon historical mining knowledge, while advanced techniques reveal the full extent of Afghanistan's lithium potential.`,
        icon: Zap,
        alignment: 'right'
      },
      {
        title: 'Battery Production & Energy Transition Impact',
        content: `Lithium reserves position Afghanistan as critical supplier for global battery production, supporting electric vehicle manufacturing and renewable energy storage. Battery-grade lithium chemicals produced from Afghan reserves will supply global markets, supporting the transition to clean energy. The strategic importance of lithium reserves extends beyond economic value, positioning Afghanistan as essential partner in global energy transition. Modern processing facilities will transform raw spodumene into battery-grade lithium carbonate and hydroxide, capturing value throughout supply chains while supporting global clean energy goals.`,
        icon: Rocket,
        alignment: 'left'
      }],
