        content: `Travel records from the 17th century document robust overland trade with thousands of camels and travelers utilizing these caravanserais. The trade volumes demonstrate the economic significance of caravan routes, with extensive commercial activity supporting regional economies. Afghan traders were active players across Asia and beyond, maintaining independent commercial networks critical to regional economic and political stability. The thousands of camels indicate substantial trade volumes, with caravan trade representing major economic activity. The independent commercial networks demonstrate Afghan merchants' role in regional trade, maintaining connections across empires and regions. Source: 17th century travel records; Trade volume documentation; Merchant network records.`,
