        content: `The first-century merchant guide Periplus Maris Erythraei documents Kushan Empire (ca. 50-200 CE) engagement in western Indian Ocean maritime trade networks. The Periplus provides detailed information about trade routes, ports, and commodities, including Afghan products reaching maritime markets. The guide demonstrates Afghanistan's connection to Red Sea and Persian Gulf maritime networks during the 1st century CE, with commodities from Afghanistan holding prominent place in western Indian Ocean trade. The Periplus represents earliest written documentation of Afghanistan's maritime trade connections, providing foundation for understanding ancient trade networks. Source: Periplus Maris Erythraei (1st century CE); Kushan Empire maritime networks.`,
