        content: `Data reports underpin quantitative timeline entries: resource estimates (12.5M t, 2.2B t, 215M t LCE), production volumes, trade, and employment. Economic impact analysis uses revenue, employment, and multiplier estimates drawn from data reports and project feasibility studies. Cross-checks with primary sources (e.g. USGS publications, ministry reports) support accuracy. Timeline entries that state numbers cite the appropriate data report or assessment so that the narrative is traceable. Production statistics, economic impact, workforce statistics, and trade volumes timeline entries depend on data reports for their figures. Consistency is maintained so that the same resource or production number does not appear with different values in different entries.`,
