        content: `Artisanal activity spans lapis, emerald, gold, coal, and other minerals. Regional variation is significant: Badakhshan and Panjshir are gemstone-focused; northern coal districts have different labor and commodity dynamics; gold is widespread. Provincial and mineral timeline entries document this variation. Data quality varies—gemstone employment is often estimated; coal production may be partially reported. The timeline reflects regional and commodity diversity so that artisanal mining is not presented as a single homogeneous sector. Cross-references to mining-communities, mining-techniques, and cultural-heritage provide fuller context.`,
