        title: 'Ancient and Traditional Techniques',
        content: `Early lapis and gem mining used hand tools, fire-setting (heating rock to fracture), and simple processing (sorting, cutting). Traditional knowledge remains relevant in artisanal sectors in Badakhshan, Panjshir, and other gemstone regions. Badakhshan and Panjshir traditions are documented in lapis-history, emerald-history, and artisanal-mining entries. Ancient techniques are inferred from archaeology and from continuity in artisanal practice. The timeline does not present ancient techniques as primitive in a negative sense but as effective for the deposit type and scale; modern artisanal miners still use variants of these methods where appropriate. Technology evolution (technology-evolution entry) and mining-tools (tools over time) provide complementary detail.`,
