        content: `Soviet geological campaigns introduced systematic drilling, blasting, and mapping; some development (e.g. chromite, coal) used Soviet-era equipment and methods. Modern feasibility studies and development plans for Mes Aynak, Hajigak, and Ghazni lithium envisage large-scale mechanized mining and processing. Timeline entries for Soviet period and modern era cover technique evolution in detail. Link to exploration-methods (how deposits are found and defined) and technology-evolution (how equipment and process have changed). Safety and environmental standards (mining-safety, environmental-factors) are part of the technique narrative so that evolution is understood as including safety and environmental improvement.`,
