        title: 'Ancient and Medieval: Egypt, Mesopotamia, Islamic Courts',
        content: `Lapis in Egyptian and Mesopotamian context and gem use in Islamic courts are documented in ancient-egypt, lapis-history, and medieval timeline entries. Tutankhamun's mask (1323 BCE) is the most cited example; Mesopotamian artifacts from Ur Dynasty (2100 BCE) and other sites show cylinder seals, jewelry, and statuettes. Islamic court use of Afghan lapis and emerald is documented in medieval-period and silk-road entries. Specific examples are cited with dates and context so that users can trace the elite use narrative. Royal and elite use established the premium status of Afghan stones and created demand that sustained trade routes over thousands of kilometers.`,
        icon: Crown,
