        title: 'Strategic Context: Magnets, Batteries, Defense',
        content: `REE are critical for permanent magnets (wind turbines, EVs), batteries, defense applications, and green energy. Afghanistan's REE timeline is part of the national strategic minerals narrative and aligns with global interest in diversifying supply away from dominant producers. Alignment with $30T+ endowment and critical minerals policy (roadmap, Vision 2026-2040) is explicit. The strategic context helps investors and policymakers understand why REE are prioritized alongside lithium and other technology metals. Applications (magnets, batteries, defense) are noted so that non-specialists can see the link between Afghan geology and end uses.`,
