        content: `Legends support intangible heritage and education. They make the human and cultural dimension of mining visible—not just deposits and production but the stories people tell. Balance between factual timeline and cultural narrative is maintained: legends are not presented as evidence for resource size or chronology but as part of heritage. Education use includes schools, heritage programs, and public outreach. Integration with cultural-heritage (identity, craft) and mining-communities (who tells the stories) provides full context.`,
        icon: Landmark,
        alignment: 'right'
