    overview: `Mining governance evolved from customary and royal control to colonial and Soviet-era regulation and to the modern Mining Law and investment framework. Historical periods had varying degrees of central control and local custom; colonial and Soviet periods introduced formal licensing and state ownership. Current law (Mining Law 2018, as amended) and regulations are summarized in investment and roadmap entries; mining-regulations and licensing-permits provide detail. Timeline entries document key legal and policy milestones (law adoption, EITI, contract signings). Bilateral investment treaties (BITs) provide investment protection. Fiscal terms and dispute resolution are noted. Integration with investment-flows and international-partnerships.`,
